                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                {
"thoughts": "Based on the information gathered, it seems that the bug may be related to the comparison logic in the assertPrintNode method. To address this, we should modify the comparison logic in the assertPrintNode method to ensure accurate comparisons between expected and actual JavaScript output.",
"command": {
"name": "write_fix",
"args": {
"project_name": "Closure",
"bug_index": 145,
"changes_dicts": [
{
"file_name": "com/google/javascript/jscomp/CodePrinterTest.java",
"insertions": [
{
"line_number": 958,
"new_lines": [
"    public void assertPrintNode(String expectedJs, Node ast) {",
"        // Get the actual output by calling the printNode's print method",
"        String actualOutput = printNode(ast);",
"        // Compare the actual output with the expected output",
"        if (!actualOutput.equals(expectedJs)) {",
"            throw new AssertionError(\"Printed output does not match expected output. Expected: \" + expectedJs + \", Actual: \" + actualOutput);",
"        }",
"    }"
]
}
]
}
]
}
